.TH FIREWALL-WEB 8 "November 2026" "firewall-web 1.0.3" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
firewall-web \- local web console for the Linux firewall
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B firewall-web
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B firewall-web
starts the authenticated local web interface on the configured address and port.
The installed launcher reads its settings from
.IR /etc/firewall-web/firewall-web.env .
At startup the application performs read-only firewall discovery and selects
the owning manager, or remains inspection-only when ownership is ambiguous.
Use
.B firewall-web --detect
for a human-readable report or
.B firewall-web --detect-json
for a versioned machine-readable report.
.PP
Set
.B NFT_BACKEND
to
.BR auto ,
.BR ufw ,
.BR firewalld ,
.BR nftables ,
.BR iptables ,
or
.B inspection
to choose a persistent backend policy. Conflicting active UFW and firewalld
instances remain inspection-only unless an administrator selects one manager
and sets
.B NFT_BACKEND_ACK
to the exact
.B conflict_acknowledgement
shown by
.BR --detect-json .
Acknowledgement does not disable, flush, migrate, or change persistence for
another manager.
.PP
The default listener is
.BR 127.0.0.1:5005 .
Use an SSH tunnel for remote access unless an authenticated HTTPS reverse proxy
is configured.
.SH SECURITY
Firewall modifications require the process to run as root with effective
.BR CAP_NET_ADMIN .
Without both, the interface is read-only and rejects all write requests.
Termux PRoot cannot alter the Android host firewall.
.PP
Set a private four-digit
.B NFT_SECRET
in the configuration file before starting. Do not expose the PIN-only service
to untrusted networks.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/firewall-web/firewall-web.env
Root-only runtime configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/firewall-web/firewall_web.py
Application and bundled web assets.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nft (8),
.BR iptables (8)
